to check the playbook syntax
ansible-playbook playbook.yaml --syntax-check

dryrun
ansible-playbook playbook.yaml --check

create new role
ansible-galaxy init myrole


when you create the user using
-name: Create the user
 user:
    name: dev
    state: present

this does create the home directory for the user
/home/dev

in linux when we craete the user using the useradd rak it will not craete the home directory 

we need to craet the 
useradd -m dev

and also when switching the user if you don't use the  -m it keeps the current dir so if we use the - it will show the  that user dir
su - rak


we have 
ansible_os_family  this has debian or redhat 
ansible_distribution this include all distro like ubuntu,rhel,fedora,centos,kali

basically deb and rh are parent distro

ansible-galaxy collection install amazon.aws

ansible-inventory -i inventory/aws_ec2.yaml --graph

To debug in  ansible we use 
ansible-playbook -i inventories/hosts firstplaybook.yaml -vvv

to dry run
ansible-playbook -i inventories/hosts firstplaybook.yaml --check 

ansible-inventory -i inventories/hosts --list # showes in json format all the hosts inside this file
ansible-inventory -i inventories/hosts --graph # showes graph  format all the hosts inside this file


pass the variable file
ansible-playbook --inventory inventories/aws_ec2.yaml firstplaybook.yml -e @group_vars/my_vault.yml

Create the ansible vault
ansible-vault create group_vars/aws_ec2.yaml 
Enter the secret
my_message: "This is test message from vault"
edit
You can only edit and view if secret is encrypted
By default when you create secret it encrypted.But you can decrypt but its no use bcz you can see the content when you do edit and view 
ansible-vault edit group_vars/my_vault.yml
ansible-vault view group_vars/my_vault.yml

now when you run the playbook you must do like this
ansible-playbook -i inventories/aws_ec2 firstplaybook.yaml --ask-vault-pass


To install plugin
ansible-galaxy collection install amazon-aws


serial 5 means it performs all tasks in any 5 machines first then it goes to next this will help for  ha bcz while working on any task if it fails then the next 5 will still be working .

we need "{{}}" to use the variable in anywhere inside code but not inside the debug var bcz its already expecting var


